      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think that is correct. It doesn\u0027t matter. As it is now, if the client sends a message \u003e 64k the emulator will crash. It is no different after these changes - i.e. if the emulator side doesn\u0027t understand the binary encoding it will reject the packet as a invalid header - and most likely crash because the stream will still be corrupted.\n\nThis is the reason it only encodes binary when with message is \u003e 64k - to retain compatibility with older emulators.",
      "parentUuid": "638c8b90_fc930d12",
